From 9f71fd279023d92474d48c6f1b3345bbbd9ca87e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:22:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/21] usb: xhci-mtk: shut the T-PHY down on remove

xhci_mtk_remove() halted the controller, powered the host IP down and
gated the clocks, but never called xhci_mtk_phy_shutdown(): the USB
T-PHYs stayed powered and initialized at handoff while their consumer
was gone.  ExitBootServices removes the controller via
dm_remove_devices_active() (efi_exit_boot_services), so every EFI boot
handed the OS a powered-on PHY that the next user (the Linux PHY
driver) cold-brings-up over.  The probe error path already used
xhci_mtk_phy_shutdown(); mirror it in remove, after the host IP is
powered down.

Signed-off-by: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
index ffe80c0bbdc..293cfc7e10a 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
@@ -345,6 +345,7 @@ static int xhci_mtk_remove(struct udevice *dev)
 
 	xhci_deregister(dev);
 	xhci_mtk_host_disable(mtk);
+	xhci_mtk_phy_shutdown(mtk);
 	xhci_mtk_ldos_disable(mtk);
 	clk_disable_bulk(&mtk->clks);
 
